From 05acf110a6dc9383a34085cc9efcad36c72d457a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 18:49:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v1.4.3: security-review remediation (HIGH/MEDIUM +
 quick LOW)

From the v1.4.2 multi-agent code review. Fixes apply to both build variants
except the AI Advisor items, which are RTCONFIG_REAPER_MCP-gated (MCP build
only).

Traffic Analyzer (rtrafd - both variants):
- HIGH: db_load trusted a signed nnet from the on-disk (USB/JFFS) history db;
  a negative value reached net_slot() -> netname[negative] out-of-bounds
  write. Reject out-of-range nnet; force-terminate all untrusted on-disk
  strings and normalize 'used' before any %s; guard the final ring read.
- MEDIUM: arp_mac re-opened+scanned /proc/net/arp per flow every second
  (O(flows x arp) CPU DoS from a LAN host). Load ARP once per poll into a
  cache; lookups are in-memory.
- LOW: reject a leading '-' in the ping probe target (no -f flood); validate
  nflist IPv4 octets 0..255.

Hardware QoS (rc/qos.c - both variants):
- MEDIUM: ip_range_checker validated the address before '-' but emitted the
  range upper bound (p+1) verbatim into an iptables --src-range rule; a tail
  newline could inject a mangle rule. Validate both bounds with isIPnum.

AI Advisor (rmcpd - MCP build only):
- HIGH: no socket/handshake timeout let a slow client wedge the single-
  threaded daemon and defeat the session-expiry + USB-key-removal lockdowns.
  Set SO_RCVTIMEO/SO_SNDTIMEO on the accepted fd.
- MEDIUM: any unauthenticated LAN host could trip the 5-bad-token self-kill
  and drop the owner's session. Only self-terminate on repeated bad tokens
  when a client pin is set (then only the pinned host can reach it).
- LOW: constant-time token compare (CRYPTO_memcmp); broaden get_logs
  redaction to ':' / spaced / quoted secret shapes.

Deferred LOW / defense-in-depth items are in the lean repo docs/BACKLOG.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
